-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ב/3: תשלום מענק חד פעמי בגובה 2,000 ₪ לעובדי הוראה
-- A one-off grant of 2,000 ₪ to teaching staff of the owners of secondary
-- education: who is entitled (continuous employment from 1.9.2010 to
-- 1.1.2011), pro-rating by the average position, sabbatical, maternity and
-- unpaid leave, what the grant does not count toward, and payment in
-- September 2011. It replaces circular תשע"ב/1.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשע"ב/3 תשלום מענק חד פעמי בגובה 2,000 ₪ לעובדי הוראה`

-- The corpus publishes this circular's letterhead, date (22.9.2011),
-- reference number and addressee as body paragraphs of an untitled block
-- (hc_1), and drops the page's section numbers 1 and 2.
-- akn:hc_1/p1 The letterhead ("מדינת ישראל"); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p2 The letterhead (the Ministry); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p3 The letterhead (the teaching-staff administration); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p4 The letterhead (the senior division of teaching personnel); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p5 The circular's title; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p6 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p7 The date, 22/09/2011; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p8 The reference number; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p9 The addressee, the owners of educational institutions; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p10 The circular's purpose: to publish the instructions for the one-off grant of 2,000 ₪; the instructions follow.
-- akn:hc_1/p11 Other changes in salary and conditions are to be published later; no rule here.
-- akn:hc_1/p12 The heading "תחולה" (scope); no rule of its own.

-- Time is counted in school months of 2011/12 (common.l4: September 2011 = 1).

@desc An absence during the determining period (1.9.2010–1.1.2011) that sections 2(ה)–(ז) deal with.
DECLARE `absence in the determining period` IS ONE OF
    `no such absence`
    `a sabbatical year for part of the period`
    `maternity leave under section 6 of the Women's Work Law`
    `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave`

@desc A teaching employee at one employer, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `grant employee` HAS
    `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011` IS A BOOLEAN @desc received the same one-off grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011 and the Wage Commissioner's circulars 2010-1-48 and 2010-1-58
    `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed continuously at the employers through the determining period, apart from the absences of sections 2(ה)–(ו)
    `absence`                            IS AN `absence in the determining period`
    `longest continuous salaried period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc in 1.9.2010–31.8.2011, the longest run of months, continuous, for which the employee was entitled to salary from the employer (4 months and a day is a little over 4)
    `average position`                   IS A NUMBER @desc the representative monthly average of the position at this employer over the part of 1.9.2010–31.8.2011 actually employed (1 = one full position)

DECLARE `grant action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the one-off grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER

§§ `1 תחולה`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_a
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this circular applies to` g IF
        g's `in the teaching-staff grade`
    AND g's `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry`

-- Section 1(ב): an employee who received the one-off grant under the
-- agreement of 25.1.2011 and the Wage Commissioner's circulars 2010-1-48 and
-- 2010-1-58 is not entitled to it a second time under this circular.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_b
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not entitled to the grant a second time` g IF
    g's `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011`

-- Section 1(ג): nothing in this circular bears on the continued
-- implementation of the reform that applies to the employee's stage of
-- education.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_c/p1
`this circular bears on the reform's implementation` MEANS FALSE

§§ `2 מענק חד פעמי`

`the grant for a full position` MEANS 2000

-- Section 2(א): continuous employment from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011 ("the
-- determining period"). Section 2(ה): a sabbatical for part of it, with
-- continuous employment for the rest, does not disentitle. Section 2(ו):
-- maternity leave (in general 26 weeks) does not break continuity, for a
-- woman or a man who takes it; unpaid leave after it falls under 2(ז).
-- Section 2(ז): with unpaid leave in the period, the test is salary for 4
-- full months and a day at least, continuously, in 1.9.2010–31.8.2011.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_c/p2 akn:hc_1__para_c/p3 akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_a akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_e akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_f akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_g
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the employment condition` g IF
    CONSIDER g's `absence`
    WHEN `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave` THEN g's `longest continuous salaried period in months` GREATER THAN 4
    OTHERWISE g's `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011`

GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the one-off grant` g IF
        `this circular applies to` g
    AND (NOT `not entitled to the grant a second time` g)
    AND `meets the employment condition` g

-- Section 2(ב): 2,000 for a full position, the same for more than a full
-- position, and pro-rated to the average position below it. The average is
-- taken over the part of the year actually employed (2(ב), 2(ז)).
-- F-2011-12_tashab_03-a: section 2(א) entitles the employee, continuously
-- employed "אצל המעסיקים", to a grant of 2,000 ₪; section 2(ב) computes it
-- by the position "אצל המעסיק", capped at 100% there, and nothing caps the
-- total of several employers. The reading adopted: each employer pays by
-- the position held with it, as section 2(ב) computes it.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_b
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grant's position share` g IS
    min (g's `average position`) 1

@export default The one-off grant one employer pays a teaching employee under circular תשע"ב/3
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee` @desc the employee at this employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-off grant` g IS
    IF `entitled to the one-off grant` g
    THEN `the grant for a full position` TIMES `the grant's position share` g
    ELSE 0

-- Sections 2(ג)–(ד): the grant is not salary for every purpose, does not
-- count toward severance pay or the hourly value, no provident-fund
-- contributions are made on it, and it does not count toward the
-- minimum-wage top-up.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_c akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_d
GIVEN u IS A `grant use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant counts toward` u IF FALSE

@desc A use a payment may be counted toward, as sections 2(ג)–(ד) ask.
DECLARE `grant use` IS ONE OF
    `salary for every purpose`
    `severance pay`
    `the hourly value`
    `contributions to a provident fund, the study fund and a pension fund included`
    `the minimum-wage top-up`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_h/p1
GIVEN g IS A `grant employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `paying the grant with September's salary` g IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the one-off grant` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the one-off grant` g
    WITHIN `month number` September
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 2(ח): the one-off grant is paid with the September 2011 salary"

§§ `3`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_c__subpara_h/p2
`the circular this one replaces` MEANS "תשע\"ב/1"

-- akn:conclusions The contact line for questions, the sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`a teacher at 80% employed throughout` MEANS
    `grant employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011` IS FALSE
        `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011` IS TRUE
        `absence`                            IS `no such absence`
        `longest continuous salaried period in months` IS 12
        `average position`                   IS 0.8

`a teacher back from unpaid leave in March 2011` MEANS
    `grant employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011` IS FALSE
        `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011` IS FALSE
        `absence`                            IS `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave`
        `longest continuous salaried period in months` IS 6
        `average position`                   IS 1.2

`a teacher back from unpaid leave in May 2011` MEANS
    `grant employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011` IS FALSE
        `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011` IS FALSE
        `absence`                            IS `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave`
        `longest continuous salaried period in months` IS 4
        `average position`                   IS 1

#ASSERT `the one-off grant` `a teacher at 80% employed throughout` EQUALS 1600
#ASSERT `the one-off grant` `a teacher back from unpaid leave in March 2011` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the one-off grant` `a teacher back from unpaid leave in May 2011` EQUALS 0

#TRACE `paying the grant with September's salary` `a teacher at 80% employed throughout` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the one-off grant` 1600 AT 1
#TRACE `paying the grant with September's salary` `a teacher at 80% employed throughout` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the one-off grant` 1600 AT 2

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over a finite space: every absence, every combination of
-- the grade, the owner, the earlier grant and continuous employment,
-- salaried runs from 0 to 12 months in quarters around 4, and average
-- positions in tenths from 0 to 1.5.

`every absence` MEANS
    LIST `no such absence`, `a sabbatical year for part of the period`,
         `maternity leave under section 6 of the Women's Work Law`,
         `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave`
`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`runs checked` MEANS LIST 0, 3, 4, 4.04, 4.25, 6, 12
`tenths to 1.5` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 15)

GIVEN g IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, a IS AN `absence in the determining period`, m IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `grant employee`
DECIDE `a checked employee` g r c a m f IS
    `grant employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS g
        `employed by an owner of secondary education supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `received the grant under the agreement of 25.1.2011` IS r
        `employed continuously from 1.9.2010 to 1.1.2011` IS c
        `absence`                            IS a
        `longest continuous salaried period in months` IS m
        `average position`                   IS f

GIVEN e IS A `grant employee`, g IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, a IS AN `absence in the determining period`, m IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 holds for` e g r c a m f IF
    LET x MEANS `the one-off grant` e
    IN      x AT LEAST 0
        AND x AT MOST `the grant for a full position`
        AND (x GREATER THAN 0) EQUALS (    g AND (NOT r) AND f GREATER THAN 0
                                       AND (IF a EQUALS `unpaid leave, or absence treated as unpaid leave`
                                            THEN m GREATER THAN 4
                                            ELSE c))
        AND ((f LESS THAN 1) OR (NOT `entitled to the one-off grant` e) OR x EQUALS `the grant for a full position`)

-- Sections 1 and 2 over the whole space: the grant is never negative and
-- never above 2,000; it is something exactly for an employee in the grade
-- with a position who did not receive it under the agreement of 25.1.2011
-- and meets the employment test — continuous employment, or, with unpaid
-- leave, more than four months salaried in a row; a full position or more
-- is paid 2,000; and the grant never falls with a larger position.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD
                all (GIVEN r YIELD
                        all (GIVEN c YIELD
                                all (GIVEN a YIELD
                                        all (GIVEN m YIELD
                                                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                                                            `section 2 holds for` (`a checked employee` g r c a m f) g r c a m f
                                                        AND `the one-off grant` (`a checked employee` g r c a m f)
                                                            AT MOST `the one-off grant` (`a checked employee` g r c a m (f PLUS 0.1)))
                                                    `tenths to 1.5`)
                                            `runs checked`)
                                    `every absence`)
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- Sections 2(ג)-(ד): the grant counts toward none of the uses they name.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN u YIELD NOT `the grant counts toward` u)
            (LIST `salary for every purpose`, `severance pay`, `the hourly value`,
                  `contributions to a provident fund, the study fund and a pension fund included`,
                  `the minimum-wage top-up`)

-- F-2011-12_tashab_03-a over every pair of positions in tenths at two
-- employers: the two grants together exceed one full position's 2,000
-- exactly where the positions add to more than one.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN h YIELD
                        LET x MEANS `the one-off grant` (`a checked employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no such absence` 12 f)
                            y MEANS `the one-off grant` (`a checked employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no such absence` 12 h)
                        IN  (x PLUS y GREATER THAN `the grant for a full position`) EQUALS (f PLUS h GREATER THAN 1))
                    (map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 10)))
            (map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 10))

`a teacher with a full position at each of two employers draws two grants` MEANS
    LET x MEANS `the one-off grant` (`a checked employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no such absence` 12 1)
    IN  x PLUS x EQUALS 2 TIMES `the grant for a full position`
#ASSERT `a teacher with a full position at each of two employers draws two grants`
